OIDC/session and Windows ACL foundations were adapted from the organization’s
Notes application (https://github.com/oneworkspacestudio/notes), also AGPL-3.0-or-later.
No Joplin renderer, Google branding, or proprietary video assets are included.

React, TanStack Query, Lucide, hls.js, Tailwind CSS, coreos/go-oidc, oauth2,
modernc SQLite, gofrs/flock, kardianos/service and other dependencies retain
their own licenses. A dependency-derived THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt accompanies
the binary distribution. Build-tool dependencies remain recorded in lockfiles.

Optional FFmpeg and FFprobe are separate executables supplied by the operator.
They are not redistributed in this package. FFmpeg licensing depends on its
build configuration; see docs/MEDIA.md and https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html.

The sample MP4 was generated with FFmpeg’s testsrc2 filter and contains no
third-party recordings. Product screenshots use only disposable test data.

YouTube imports optionally download checksum-pinned standalone yt-dlp and Deno
directly from their upstream releases. They run as separate processes and are
not included in the My Tube binary. yt-dlp is Unlicense with separately licensed
bundled dependencies; Deno is MIT with bundled dependencies. Preserve upstream
notices: https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp and https://github.com/denoland/deno.
Version pins and source/license links are documented in docs/YOUTUBE-IMPORTS.md.
